statement:
Fix a bit-string $z \in \{0,1\}^n$, and for each $x \in \{0,1\}^n$ let $\langle x, z\rangle \in \{0,1\}$ denote the mod-2 inner product of $x$ and $z$. Summing the Boolean sign $(-1)^{\langle x, z\rangle}$ over all $2^n$ inputs $x$ gives
\[
  \sum_{x \in \{0,1\}^n} (-1)^{\langle x, z\rangle}
  \;=\;
  \begin{cases} 2^n & \text{if $z$ is the all-zero string,} \\ 0 & \text{otherwise.} \end{cases}
\]
